  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $20.4$ | $18.6$ | $16.5$ | $14.4$ | $12.3$ | $10.8$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{\u2032}(2)\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(2) & \u2248\\frac{g(2+2)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.4-16.5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.1}{2} \\\\  & =-1.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
